# tools/cl/cluster_minimum_spanning_tree_witness.rish -- the skeleton that holds a cluster layout together, on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- image/cluster_graph.rye joins the cluster-pair read over every cluster pair into one matrix;
# image/cluster_graph_profile.rye reads the whole edge-count curve as a distribution over thresholds; image/cluster_connectivity.rye reads
# WHEN the layout becomes one connected region as reach grows -- the connectivity threshold, a single number (the MST bottleneck). This rung
# reads the tree itself: the actual BRIDGE EDGES that skeleton is made of, so a surface can draw the connecting lines. Exact integers, NO
# float, NO tolerance.
#
# The crux this witness proves on metal, two shapes: THE MST IS THE SKELETON, ITS BOTTLENECK THE CONNECTIVITY THRESHOLD -- over the
# three-cluster scene (distances 2, 3, 10) the tree is a star on the hub, edges 1-2 and 1-3, never the diameter edge 2-3, its bottleneck (3)
# equal to the connectivity threshold; THE TREE DROPS THE REDUNDANT CYCLE EDGE -- over a four-cluster scene (a triangle plus a far outlier)
# the thresholded graph at reach 3 holds a whole triangle yet the MST holds exactly n-1 edges, the third triangle edge dropped because a
# spanning tree carries no cycle. A lone-cluster layout is already one whole. Determinism. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/cl/cluster_minimum_spanning_tree_witness.rish

say "cluster_minimum_spanning_tree: Language EN -- Season G the skeleton that holds a cluster layout together; build_mst grows the minimum spanning tree by Prim, mst_weight sums its bridges, mst_bottleneck reads its largest edge, edge_count its size, is_bridge whether a pair is an edge; NO float, NO tolerance."
say "cluster_minimum_spanning_tree: Style Radiant -- compose not braid: this rung owns only the spanning-tree reads (Prim's growth over the matrix, the weight sum, the bottleneck, the bridge test); cluster_graph owns the precomputed cluster matrix, cluster_connectivity owns the connectivity threshold cross-checked here never re-derived. A reading over a reading over a reading over a reading over a reading over a reading over a reading."
say "cluster_minimum_spanning_tree: Lens TAME -- the tree holds at most the cluster ceiling minus one edges, Prim's key arrays are exactly the cluster count, each of the n-1 growth rounds scans the matrix once; a zero or past-the-count cluster id refuses BadClusterId, a self pair refuses SameCluster; all-or-nothing; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/cluster_minimum_spanning_tree"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/cluster_minimum_spanning_tree.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "cluster_minimum_spanning_tree: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "cluster_minimum_spanning_tree: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "cluster_minimum_spanning_tree: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-cluster-minimum-spanning-tree" else "cluster_minimum_spanning_tree: selftest did not print the GREEN line"
assert selftest.out contains "THE MST IS THE SKELETON, ITS BOTTLENECK THE CONNECTIVITY THRESHOLD" else "cluster_minimum_spanning_tree: the skeleton case did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "a STAR on the hub cluster 1" else "cluster_minimum_spanning_tree: the star-on-the-hub fact did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "THE TREE DROPS THE REDUNDANT CYCLE EDGE" else "cluster_minimum_spanning_tree: the cycle-edge case did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "because a spanning tree carries no cycle" else "cluster_minimum_spanning_tree: the no-cycle fact did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "the skeleton and the threshold meeting at the largest edge" else "cluster_minimum_spanning_tree: the meet-at-the-largest-edge fact did not print"

say "cluster_minimum_spanning_tree: GREEN on metal -- the skeleton a surface draws to hold a scattered layout together, the actual bridge edges of a minimum spanning tree grown by Prim over the true-distance matrix, its bottleneck the connectivity threshold, exact integers with NO float and NO tolerance; the tree names which edges bridge, not only the reach at which they close."
